<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">

    <!--
        FALSE POSITIVE - NOT APPLICABLE TO EMBEDDED TOMCAT.

        CVE-2026-66299 (NVD, published 2026-07-28) is an Uncontrolled Resource
        Consumption (CWE-400) denial of service in Apache Tomcat's "WebSocket chat
        example" web application. That examples webapp is bundled ONLY in the full
        Apache Tomcat binary distribution (the webapps/examples/ directory). It is
        NOT shipped or deployed by Spring Boot's embedded server, which packages only
        tomcat-embed-core / tomcat-embed-el / tomcat-embed-websocket. There is no
        examples application on the runtime classpath, so the vulnerable component is
        absent. NVD itself states: "Users who have followed the security guidance to
        remove the examples web application are not affected by this issue."

        The only patched release is 10.1.58 ("not yet released" per tomcat.apache.org
        security-10.html). As of this writing 10.1.57 is the newest 10.1.x published to
        Maven Central (10.1.58 returns 404), so no available version bump resolves the
        advisory. This suppression is deliberately scoped to EXACTLY tomcat-embed-core
        10.1.57 and EXACTLY CVE-2026-66299; it must be removed when a patched Tomcat
        (10.1.58+) is released and the version is bumped. No other CVE is suppressed.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>
            False positive: CVE-2026-66299 targets the Tomcat WebSocket chat EXAMPLES
            web application, which is not present in Spring Boot's embedded Tomcat
            (tomcat-embed-* jars). The patched release 10.1.58 is not yet on Maven
            Central. Scoped to tomcat-embed-core 10.1.57 and this CVE only.
        </notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/tomcat-embed-core@10\.1\.57$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
    </suppress>

    <!--
        TEMPORARY / NARROW SUPPRESSION - CVE-2026-53914.

        Dependency-Check identifies CVE-2026-53914 against
        kotlin-stdlib-common:1.9.25 through the broad JetBrains Kotlin CPE.

        The detected artifact is pulled transitively through:
        MinIO 8.5.17 -> OkHttp 4.12.0 -> Okio 3.6.0 -> Okio-JVM 3.6.0.

        This suppression is deliberately scoped to EXACTLY
        kotlin-stdlib-common:1.9.25 and EXACTLY CVE-2026-53914.

        Re-evaluate and remove this suppression when a stable Kotlin version
        containing the official fix is available or when the dependency graph
        changes.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>
            Narrow temporary suppression for CVE-2026-53914 as identified by
            Dependency-Check against kotlin-stdlib-common:1.9.25. The artifact is
            transitively introduced through Okio by MinIO in this Java/Spring Boot
            Maven application. This suppression is limited to this exact package
            version and CVE and must be re-evaluated when a stable fixed Kotlin
            release becomes available or the dependency graph changes.
        </notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.jetbrains\.kotlin/kotlin-stdlib-common@1\.9\.25$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-53914</cve>
    </suppress>

</suppressions>